---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Mailbox Atlas';
const description = 'Virtual mailbox prices, scan and forwarding fees, and USPS Form 1583 rules compared, with a source link on every number.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} updated="2026-11-20">
  <h1>Virtual mailboxes, priced out</h1>
  <p class="lede">What a virtual mailbox really costs once scans, forwarding and the Form 1583 notary are added. Every number is copied from the provider's own page and linked to it.</p>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/virtual-mailbox-pricing-comparison/">Pricing compared</a></h3><p>Eight providers: plans, mail allowances, scan and forwarding fees.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/cheapest-virtual-mailbox/">The cheapest virtual mailbox</a></h3><p>From $4.99, and when the cheap plan stops being cheap.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/usps-form-1583-online-notarization/">Form 1583 &amp; online notary</a></h3><p>What USPS requires, and which providers skip the notary.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/traveling-mailbox-vs-postscan-mail/">Traveling Mailbox vs PostScan Mail</a></h3><p>Fee by fee, with a worked monthly example.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/ipostal1-vs-anytime-mailbox/">iPostal1 vs Anytime Mailbox</a></h3><p>One national price list vs 2,000+ operator-set plans.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/ipostal1-pricing/">iPostal1 pricing explained</a></h3><p>All 12 tiers, address surcharges and every per-use fee.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/anytime-mailbox-pricing/">Anytime Mailbox pricing</a></h3><p>Starting prices of all 2,095 U.S. locations, and why they differ.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/virtual-mailbox-for-llc/">Virtual mailbox for an LLC</a></h3><p>Registered office vs mailing address, and plans that bundle an agent.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><a href="/virtual-mailbox-check-deposit-fees/">Check deposit fees</a></h3><p>From free to $10 a check, provider by provider.</p></div>
  </div>
</Base>
